          "actorPermissionLevel": "LIMITED_PERMISSIONS",
          "readmeSummary": "## Threads Scraper\n\nA scraper for Threads (threads.com) that extracts profiles, user posts, replies, and single-post reply threads without requiring a login, cookies, or an account. It bootstraps a public guest token from Threads' web app and calls Threads' public GraphQL API over plain HTTP to fetch and normalize data into a stable, flat schema. Outputs are record-level rows containing post text, engagement counts (likes/replies/reposts/quotes), media information (images/videos and their URLs), timestamps, canonical post URLs and identifiers, author/profile metadata (name, follower metrics, verification, bio, profile image), link preview targets, and optionally users who liked a post. Designed for structured export and downstream analysis, monitoring, or feeding into AI agents; supports use of datacenter or residential proxies for higher-volume scraping.\n\n## Use cases\n\n- Scrape entire account timelines to collect all posts from one or more Threads profiles in a single run.  \n- Retrieve replies authored by specified users across Threads.  \n- Extract profile metadata such as full name, follower counts, biography, verification status, and profile picture.  \n- Fetch a single Threads post and its full reply thread for conversation analysis.  \n- Collect post-level details (text, engagement metrics, media, timestamps, link previews) for monitoring, analytics, or training models.  \n- Optionally gather the list of users who liked a specific post for social graph or engagement research.",
